{"_meta":{"com.oxinsider/docs-group":"markets","securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["read"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Get market closing line"},"description":"The closing line of one sports or esports market: the price Polymarket's own price-history series recorded for each outcome in the last minute bucket that ended at or before kickoff, read once after the market settles and stored unchanged. Not a midpoint and not a last trade. outcomes[0] is the YES leg as stored; outcomes[1] is the NO leg, 1 minus the YES price (derived_from_yes true). status is measured with both legs; pending when no close is stored yet (the game has not started, the market has not settled, or the capture has not reached it; it measures markets up to 30 days after kickoff); or unavailable with unavailable_reason when none will be served. A missing close is never 0. anchor_stale is true when kickoff has moved more than lookback_seconds since capture. The same close measures the clv object on each large trade.\n\nArgs:\n  - condition_id (string, required): Raw provider condition_id or the mkt_-prefixed market id\n\nReturns: condition_id, status, unavailable_reason, game_start_time, close_anchor_at, close_anchor_source, anchor_stale, lookback_seconds, observed_at, observation_window_seconds, price_source, basis_version, captured_at, outcomes (outcome_index, outcome, token_id, close_price, derived_from_yes) and meta.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"condition_id":{"description":"Raw provider condition_id or the mkt_-prefixed market id","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["condition_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_market_close","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"MarketClose":{"properties":{"anchor_stale":{"type":["boolean","null"]},"basis_version":{"type":["string","null"]},"captured_at":{"format":"date-time","type":["string","null"]},"close_anchor_at":{"format":"date-time